    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d660">

                <pb facs="0715" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg457"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857Ar5/2</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-30T16:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 30, 1915, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.30 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2378. Consul at Bristol reports that British authorities state <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Armenian</hi> of Leyland Line from Newport News to
                    British port has been torpedoed and sunk by German submarine <hi
                        rendition="#italic">U–38</hi> off Cornwall. Consul reports twenty-one
                    Americans lost. British Admiralty informs me that ship was engaged on Admiralty
                    business and understands she carried no passengers. Americans lost therefore
                    appear to be members of crew.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
